  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{刷|さつ} (print, renew) + {新|しん} (new)\nLiterally \"renew-new\" - emphasizes making something completely fresh.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {刷新|さっしん}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{図|はか}る→図る：12006_hakaru⟧ - to aim for reform\n- {刷新|さっしん}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{行|おこな}う→行う：01238_okonau⟧ - to carry out reform\n- ⟦{人事|じんじ}→人事：00126_jinji⟧{刷新|さっしん} - personnel overhaul\n- ⟦イメージ→イメージ：03832_imeeji⟧{刷新|さっしん} - image renewal\n- ⟦{組織|そしき}→組織：03320_soshiki⟧{刷新|さっしん} - organizational reform\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{改革|かいかく}→改革：04815_kaikaku⟧ - reform (broader, systemic change)\n- ⟦{改善|かいぜん}→改善：00144_kaizen⟧ - improvement (incremental)\n- ⟦{一新|いっしん}→一新：19941_isshin⟧ - complete renewal\n- ⟦{革新|かくしん}→革新：05617_kakushin⟧ - innovation, revolution\n\nUSAGE:\n{刷新|さっしん} implies sweeping away the old and replacing it with something entirely new. Stronger than ⟦{改善|かいぜん}→改善：00144_kaizen⟧ but less radical than ⟦{革命|かくめい}→革命：05968_kakumei⟧.",
